Day 30 - AWS IAM Fundamentals

Topics learned:

- Identity and Access Management (IAM)
- IAM Users
- IAM Groups
- IAM Policies
- IAM Roles
- Principle of Least Privilege
- Root User vs IAM User

What I learned:

- IAM controls access to AWS resources.
- Users represent individuals.
- Groups simplify permission management.
- Policies define allowed and denied actions.
- Roles provide temporary permissions to AWS services.
- The root account should not be used for everyday tasks.
- Security is improved by granting only the permissions required.
